  geom_histogram(bins = 30, fill = "steelblue", color = "white") +
  labs(title = "Natural log of heavy-rail station ridership",
       x = "ln(Ridership)", y = "Stations") + theme_minimal(base_family='roboto') 
```

```{r}
#| label: q6-summary
summary(hrt_pos$rider);    sd(hrt_pos$rider)
summary(hrt_pos$ln_rider); sd(hrt_pos$ln_rider)
```

The first distribution of heavy-rail station ridership is right-skewed, meaning that most of the data falls in lower values. The second distribution of the natural log of heavy-rail station ridership is roughly normally distributed, with data clustering around the central mean. Taking the natural log of ridership transforms the data (a "log-transformation") from a skewed distribution into a natural distribution.

