## Question 9

Ridership as a function of population and jobs within a half mile, terminal status, and airport connection.

```{r}
#| label: q9-lm
m1 <- lm(rider ~ pop_halfmile + jobs_halfmile + terminal_d + airport_d, data = hrt)
summary(m1)
```

In this OLS regression model, the predictors all have a positive linear association. That is, for each one-unit increase in the predictor, the dependent variable increases by 1. All predictors besides `airport_d` are statistically significant. The predictor with the largest magnitude is `terminal_d`, followed by `airport_d`, `jobs_halfmile` and `pop_halfmile`.

